      "prompt_sha1": "5a28af44cc22d8ec0e8633428410b75b8b0ee6ad",
      "answer": "GPT-4 was fine-tuned using supervised learning (SFT) with demonstration data to imitate the behavior in the demonstrations [D3]. Additionally, a reward model (RM) was trained using ranking data to predict the average labeler’s preference for a given output, which was then used as a reward signal for reinforcement learning (specifically, the PPO algorithm) to further fine-tune the model [D3]. This process aimed to steer the model towards the desired behavior by rewarding specific outputs [D3]. The fine-tuning process also involved post-training alignment to improve performance on measures of factuality and adherence to desired behavior [D4].",
